# Dr. Denys Dutykh (Mathematics Department, Khalifa University of Science and Technology, Abu Dhabi, UAE)
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the article that it accompanies."
type: software
title: "kernel-poisson: kernel Poisson regression with exposures"
abstract: >-
  Kernel Poisson and negative-binomial regression with exposures: the estimator, its Newton
  solver with Fisher-weighted landmarks, leave-one-out tuning in closed form, the competitors
  of the benchmark and the ten open data sets, with the code that rebuilds every figure and
  table of the article.
